coder › Done, on branch `feat/wrap` (two commits, working tree clean).

**What I changed**

`src/wrap.ts` — implemented `wrap(text, width)`:
- `width < 1` throws `RangeError` up front.
- Input is split on `"\n\n"` into paragraphs; each is word-wrapped independently, then rejoined with `"\n\n"`, so exactly one blank line separates paragraphs. Empty paragraphs are dropped, which collapses runs of blank lines to one.
- Within a paragraph, words come from `split(/\s+/)` with empties filtered, so runs of spaces (and newlines inside a paragraph) count as one separator. Leading/trailing spaces vanish.
- Greedy line filling: a word is appended when `line.length + 1 + word.length <= width`, otherwise the line is flushed. Lines never end in a space because words are joined with a single `"`"` only when a space fits.
- A word longer than `width` flushes the current line and is sliced into `width`-character chunks; the final partial chunk stays on the last line and can absorb following words if they fit.
- Empty input (or an all-blank input) returns `""`.

`src/wrap.test.ts` — 16 tests in `bun test` style: greedy filling, space runs, long-word splitting, paragraphs and blank-line runs, trailing-space and width-cap invariants over several widths, idempotence, empty/blank input, `RangeError` cases.

**Checks, exact output**

```
